# Responsive UI (hard)

Every UI surface must work from mobile through desktop. Desktop-only layouts are banned.

## Breakpoints ([docs/design-system.md](../../docs/design-system.md) §18)

| Token | Min-width | Use |
| ----- | --------- | --- |
| `sm`  | 640px     | Mobile → tablet adjustments |
| `md`  | 768px     | Table layout |
| `lg`  | 1000px    | Two-column / sidebar |
| `xl`  | 1280px    | Max content width |

## Required

- Mobile-first: base = small viewport; enhance with `sm:` / `md:` / `lg:` / `xl:`
- Shell padding: `px-4 sm:px-6` (16px → 24px); content `max-w-7xl`
- No horizontal overflow — use `min-w-0`, `truncate`, `shrink-0` in flex rows
- Hide/reflow secondary chrome on small screens (`max-sm:hidden`); keep primary nav/actions usable
- Verify ~375px and desktop before done (Playwright / browser when UI is involved)

## Banned

- Fixed widths that overflow small screens
- Hover-only UI with no keyboard/touch path
- Skipping responsive work because “MVP is desktop”

